<title>USA: Duff &amp; Phelps rates $1 bln Argentina bond offering.</title>
<headline>Duff &amp; Phelps rates $1 bln Argentina bond offering.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Wednesday it assigned a Double B rating to a US$1 billion global bond offering from the Republic of Argentina.</p>
<p>The bonds come due October 2006.</p>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps said it revised its GDP growth forecast for 1996 to 3.1 percent from 2.2 percent based on better than expected provisional GDP growth in the second quarter.</p>
<p>Argentina has a higher fiscal deficit than the original target for 1996. However, it has responded with revenue enhancement measures and spending freezes to offset fiscal deterioration, Duff &amp; Phelps said.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
